{
  "year": 2011,
  "pointsSystem": "2011 Reebok CrossFit Games 100-point scoring table. The event winner earned 100 points; points then dropped 5 per place through 6th (100, 95, 90, 85, 80, 75), 2 points per place from 7th through 30th (73, 71, 69, 67, 65, 63 ... 27), and 1 point per place beyond 30th (26, 25, 24, 23, 22 ...). Each of the 10 events paid out on this same scale, and final placing is the sum of event points; ties share a placing and its points (e.g. three men tied 2nd in The End 2 at 137 reps, each earning 95). Skills 1 (Event 2) and Skills 2 (Event 5) were scored internally by summing each athlete's rank across three component tests, then paid out on the standard scale, so their score column shows event points (e.g. '100 pt'), not a raw mark - the official leaderboard preserved only the final event placing for those two events.",
